# What the application package ships, and where.
#
# EVERYTHING GOES UNDER /opt/tt-bio-demo, not into dist-packages. These are
# not libraries anyone should import: `ui` and `runner` are two halves of one
# application that run under two DIFFERENT interpreters (venv-ui has GTK and
# no torch; venv-runner has torch/ttnn and no GTK -- see the project's
# CLAUDE.md), and `protocol` is deliberately importable by both. Installing
# `ui/` or `protocol/` into the system Python would put three top-level names
# that generic on every Python path on the machine.
#
# Listed directory by directory rather than as a glob of the repo root. A
# glob would ship tests/, .venvs/, generated/, recordings/ and the docs tree
# the first time someone added one -- and a package that quietly grows is one
# nobody notices growing. `test_tests_and_scratch_do_not_ship` is what holds
# this line.

ui                  opt/tt-bio-demo/
runner              opt/tt-bio-demo/
protocol            opt/tt-bio-demo/
playlist            opt/tt-bio-demo/
examples            opt/tt-bio-demo/
scripts             opt/tt-bio-demo/
VERSION             opt/tt-bio-demo/

debian/com.tenstorrent.ttbio.demo.desktop    usr/share/applications/

# The app icon, at every size a panel or launcher asks for. Until now the
# desktop entry said `Icon=tt-bio-demo` and NOTHING shipped that name, so every
# launcher fell back to a generic placeholder -- the entry referenced an icon
# that did not exist. `test_the_desktop_entry_names_an_icon_that_ships` is what
# holds this line now.
#
# The artwork is the Ctrl+G easter egg: the Tenstorrent mark as the point cloud
# a chip descends into. Sizes 64 and up keep the dots; 48 and below are a solid
# silhouette of the same shape, because a point cloud is illegible at 16px.
assets/icons/hicolor          usr/share/icons/
# Icon basenames are the app ID, matching the desktop file. A launcher
# resolves Icon= through the icon theme by exact name, so the two must agree.

# helpers.sh lives in the BASE package, which tt-bio-demo-runtime and
# tt-bio-demo-weights both depend on. It used to be shipped by BOTH of those,
# to the same path -- two packages owning one file, which dpkg refuses when
# they are installed together. Here it is owned once.
debian/helpers.sh             usr/share/tt-bio-demo/

# NOTE the unit is NOT listed here. It is debian/tt-bio-demo.user.service and
# dh_installsystemduser places it in /usr/lib/systemd/user/. Naming it
# `tt-bio-demo.service` made dh_installsystemd ALSO claim it by filename
# convention and install a second copy as a SYSTEM unit -- which the spec
# rejects and `test_the_unit_is_a_user_service_not_a_system_one` caught.
